.TH NOXFORGE-DOCTOR 1 "September 2026" "NoxForge 12.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
noxforge-doctor \- inspect a NoxForge installation without changing it
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B noxforge-doctor
.RB [ \-\-json ]
.RB [ \-\-root
.IR path ]
.RB [ \-\-remediation-plan ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B noxforge-doctor
reports the installed package version, component provenance and versions,
safely readable active theme names, icon inheritance, actual per-output scales,
and the effective login surface when it can be detected.
It does not write files, apply a theme, clear caches, restart services, switch
display managers, or request privileges.
.PP
JSON schema 5 retains stable
.B edition
and
.B loginSurface
objects. The latter reports the manager, service state, integration type,
asset availability, selection, and status. An installed SDDM theme is not
reported as active when Plasma Login Manager is active. Unselected optional
login assets do not make the installation incomplete. Schema 5 also discovers
GTK 3/4 themes, KSyntaxHighlighting themes, terminal/editor assets, and the
Flatpak theme-override readiness state, while reporting fractional display
scales when available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit machine-readable JSON.
.TP
.BI \-\-root " path"
Inspect an absolute staged or system root instead of the running system.
.TP
.B \-\-remediation-plan
Emit a non-destructive shell plan for the detected state. The plan is advice
only; the command preserves the report's status-derived exit code and does not
execute the suggested actions.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command help.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Returns 0 for a complete, version-consistent installation, 1 for an absent,
partial, or mixed-version installation, and 2 for invalid command arguments.
.SH PRIVACY
The report omits usernames, hostnames, and display contents. User component
paths use the $XDG_DATA_HOME prefix; staged paths are shown as supplied.
It never treats QT_SCALE_FACTOR as per-output evidence.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/noxforge/VERSION
Expected installed NoxForge version.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rpm (8),
.BR dnf (8)

.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Components include ordered discovered paths, effective and shadowed data paths,
per-copy versions, metadata availability, and duplicate classification.
Identical component payloads warn without failing; conflicting payloads fail
even when versions match. Native plugin paths are candidates, not proof of the
runtime loader choice. Structured issues and text output share one assessment.
Standalone components require only their declared dependencies. The global theme
requires all portable components. Portable and system editions require their
component set, with edition-specific repair advice.
.PP
An alternate root never falls back to source VERSION or host session settings.
Missing version metadata is explicitly unknown. No duplicate is removed.
